**Where the repair fell short**

The trim landed at 67 words net, not the 500 to 900 the verifier asked for. The structural asks were all applied: the three Type 3 exhibits are quoted once with back-references in the Type 7 and Type 6 sections, the dense Type 6 section is split into three paragraphs, the "wants" and "hurts" paragraphs are merged, and "this profile" hedges in the body dropped from seven to four. A larger cut would have removed inventoried claims or reviewer-protected passages that the same acceptance test requires to stay. The resolution states this plainly with the exact figures, so the next verifier can judge it.

